Keeps `data/` present in a fresh clone.

`data/manifest.json` used to do this incidentally -- it was the only tracked file here, and it
went with the curated corpus. Without something tracked, `git clone` produces no `data/` at all,
and `docker-compose.yml`'s `../data:/app/data` bind mount then makes Docker create it **owned by
root**. The images run as a non-root `appuser`, so the first upload fails with a permission error
that points at the application rather than at a missing directory.

Everything actually written here (uploads/, processed/) is gitignored.
